# 23 -- per-dataset validation targets: PC_ERMSE (i).
#
# Example 01 without PC_LAMMPS, validated on two datasets instead of one:
# the local config.val lists the elastic set (1) and the bcc
# equation-of-state set (2), and common/run.sh uses it in place of
# ../common/config.val. Each dataset gets its own target and weight.
# The EOS set's RMSE is about 2.8x smaller than the elastic set's, so it
# is weighted 10x, which makes its term comparable to the elastic one in
# the L2 loss (about 1.3x it at the optimum). loss.tadah and
# stats.tadah get one column per dataset (L(ERMSE)[1], L(ERMSE)[2]);
# with indexed targets the reported L(ERMSE)[avg] is the average of the
# dataset losses.
#
# --skip-above 5 on dataset 2 is a per-dataset bad-potential filter: a
# candidate whose EOS error exceeds 5 meV/atom scores FAILSCORE and skips
# the rest of its evaluation. In this box that is RCUT2B below about
# 4.07 A (5.7 meV/atom at 4.0 A). This run's path (RCUT2B 5.6 to 6.0,
# 1.7 to 1.9 meV/atom) never goes there, so the filter does not fire here.

OPTIMIZER
  STRATEGY
    TYPE PLAIN
    LIB DLIB
    ALGO BFGS
    MAXEVAL 30
  ENDSTRATEGY
ENDOPTIMIZER

LOSS L2
FAILSCORE 1e16
PC_ERMSE (1) 0 1e-4
PC_ERMSE (2) 0 1e-3 --skip-above 5

OPTIM RCUT2B (1) 4.0 6.0

OUTPUT 1
BOUTPUT 1
